// Module `float`: f32 and f64 (SEM-2). CORE operations (mul_add, to_i64 and siblings,
// total_order) are in core.md. `T` ranges over the float types. Nothing here allocates.

/// Parses the whole of s as a decimal float: optional '-', digits with an optional
/// fraction, an optional exponent (JSON number syntax; "inf" and "nan" are refused).
/// Correctly rounded (round-to-nearest-even). A value too large for T is Ok(infinity);
/// callers that need a finite number test `float.is_finite`.
/// Fails: Error(Empty | Invalid(i)). Alloc: nothing; the slow path keeps at most 768
/// significant digits in a fixed-size local record, as Rust's dec2flt does.
/// Cost: O(len); Eisel-Lemire fast path, big-decimal slow path linear in the digits.
/// Ex: `let x: f64 = float.parse(token)?`
pub fn parse[T](s: String) -> Result[T, int.ParseError]

/// Whether x is neither infinite nor NaN. Cost: O(1). Ex: `float.is_finite(x)`
pub fn is_finite[T](x: T) -> bool
